  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Careless Whisper** (1 review): The Wham cover starts with audible crowd laughter, highlighting the audience's humor [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Isn't It A Pity**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **Rocket Man**: back after 208 archived shows (3962 days); rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **It Makes No Difference**: back after 116 archived shows (2220 days); rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **Careless Whisper**: back after 88 archived shows (2022 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2012-07-14.mk21.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 22 songs; 149 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: The audio is slightly muffled, though the overall performance quality is high; The recording quality is described as amazing and worthy of repeated listening [2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Preservation Hall Jazz Band joined as guests on the track Holdin On To Black Metal [6]\n- The twenty-two song set was a celebration hosted in the band's hometown [6]\n- The guest-filled set was livestreamed on Friday night from Louisville [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2012-07-14.mk21.flac16**: taped by Brian Porter; source: Schoeps mk21 (ORTF/FOB) > kcy > Sonosax SX-M2-LS2 > Sony M10 (24/48) [1]. Also: The taping was done by Brian, as noted by the reviewer [4]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by JamBase: [Full Show Friday | My Morning Jacket & Guests At Forecastle](https://www.jambase.com/article/full-show-friday-my-morning-jacket-guests-at-forecastle) [8]",
